    "text": "Q: Enumerate how the transport layer ensure that the complete message arrives at the destination and in the proper order(AKTU 2016-17, 2017-18) The transport layer in the OSI and TCP/IP models ensures that a complete message arrives at the destination accurately and in the proper order using the following mechanisms: 1. Segmentation and Reassembly 2. Sequencing 3. Acknowledgments (ACKs) 4. Error Detection and Correction 5. Retransmission (Automatic Repeat request - ARQ) 6. Flow Control (e.g., Sliding Window Protocol) 7. Connection Establishment and Termination (for TCP) These functions are primarily handled by TCP (Transmission Control Protocol).",
